{"messages":[{"content":"Work through the provided tools to repair the project according to the task.\nExisting source files may be edited; tests are read-only. outline provides Python\nstructure; read_file provides exact numbered source. verify runs the fixed tests\nand returns full results in every condition. finish ends your attempt; acceptance\nis evaluated separately on a fresh snapshot using the original tests.\nAutomatic conditions run those same tests synchronously after each successful\nsource-changing edit. Check receipts and failures describe the check, not task\nacceptance. An unchanged edit or rejected edit does not run a hook. An execution\nerror, timeout or stale check must be investigated. Full evidence handles can be\nretrieved through read_output/search_output. Choose economical steps; finish once\nyou have evidence your implementation satisfies the task.\n\nCondition: No automatic checks. Invoke verify when useful.\nTask: Fix billing so sales tax is calculated on the amount remaining after discounts. Preserve existing checkout, shipping, and discount behavior.\nFiles: checkout.py, models.py, pricing.py, test_contract.py","role":"system"},{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"path\": \"pricing.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Pricing and tax calculation service.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom typing import Dict, Optional\\nfrom models import Cart, PromoCode\\n\\n\\nSTATE_TAX_RATES: Dict[str, float] = {\\n    \\\"CA\\\": 0.0825,  # 8.25%\\n    \\\"NY\\\": 0.08875, # 8.875%\\n    \\\"TX\\\": 0.0625,  # 6.25%\\n    \\\"WA\\\": 0.065,   # 6.5%\\n    \\\"OR\\\": 0.0,     # No sales tax\\n    \\\"DE\\\": 0.0,     # No sales tax\\n}\\n\\nDEFAULT_TAX_RATE = 0.05\\nFREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD = 150.0\\nSTANDARD_SHIPPING_FEE = 15.0\\n\\n\\ndef get_tax_rate(state: str) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Returns state sales tax rate.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return STATE_TAX_RATES.get(state.upper(), DEFAULT_TAX_RATE)\\n\\n\\ndef calculate_volume_discount(subtotal: float) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Applies tiered volume discount.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if subtotal >= 500.0:\\n        return 0.10  # 10% off\\n    elif subtotal >= 300.0:\\n        return 0.05  # 5% off\\n    return 0.0\\n\\n\\ndef calculate_shipping(subtotal: float) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Free shipping over $150, otherwise flat fee.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if subtotal >= FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD:\\n        return 0.0\\n    return STANDARD_SHIPPING_FEE\\n\\n\\ndef compute_discount_amount(\\n    subtotal: float,\\n    promo: Optional[PromoCode] = None\\n) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Calculates total discount dollars from volume or promo code.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    discount_pct = 0.0\\n    if promo and promo.is_eligible(subtotal):\\n        discount_pct = max(discount_pct, promo.discount_percent)\\n    else:\\n        discount_pct = max(discount_pct, calculate_volume_discount(subtotal))\\n\\n    return round(subtotal * discount_pct, 2)\\n\\n\\ndef calculate_final_bill(\\n    cart: Cart,\\n    state: str,\\n    promo: Optional[PromoCode] = None\\n) -> Dict[str, float]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Computes full breakdown: subtotal, discount, tax, shipping, final total.\\n\\n    Rule: Sales tax must only be assessed on the post-discount taxable amount.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    subtotal = cart.subtotal\\n    discount_amount = compute_discount_amount(subtotal, promo)\\n    discounted_subtotal = round(subtotal - discount_amount, 2)\\n\\n    tax_rate = get_tax_rate(state)\\n\\n    tax_amount = round(discounted_subtotal * tax_rate, 2)\\n\\n    shipping_fee = calculate_shipping(discounted_subtotal)\\n    final_total = round(discounted_subtotal + tax_amount + shipping_fee, 2)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"subtotal\\\": subtotal,\\n        \\\"discount_amount\\\": discount_amount,\\n        \\\"taxable_amount\\\": discounted_subtotal,\\n        \\\"tax_amount\\\": tax_amount,\\n        \\\"shipping_fee\\\": shipping_fee,\\n        \\\"final_total\\\": final_total,\\n    }\\n\"}","name":"write_file"},"id":"control_0","type":"function"}]},{"content":"Overwrote pricing.py (2397 bytes, 85 lines).","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"control_0"}],"tools":[{"function":{"description":"Recursively list workspace-relative file paths that match a glob, in sorted order. The glob is matched against each file's relative path and against its file name, using Python fnmatch rules, case-sensitive: '*' and '?' also match '/', and '[abc]' matches one listed character. It never matches file contents. Cache and VCS directories (.git, __pycache__, .pytest_cache, .mypy_cache, .ruff_cache, .tox, .venv, node_modules) are skipped.","name":"glob_files","parameters":{"properties":{"glob":{"description":"Required. For example '*.py', 'tests/*', or 'setup.cfg'.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Directory (or single file) to list under, relative to the workspace root. Default '.'.","type":"string"}},"required":["glob"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"Read a text file with 1-based line numbers. start_line and end_line are inclusive; omit start_line to begin at line 1 and end_line to read to the end. The header reports the range returned and the file's total lines. Long results are shown partially with an output id for paging.","name":"read_file","parameters":{"properties":{"end_line":{"type":"integer"},"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"List the classes and functions of a Python file with line numbers.","name":"outline","parameters":{"properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"Search case-sensitive literal text by default, or Python regex with regex=true. Returns one line per matching line as path:line: text, with 1-based line numbers; context_lines adds surrounding lines. file_glob only selects which files a